# Allowlist, same shape as farm_assistant_um: the adapter image needs the app
# code and the dependency manifest, nothing else.
#
# This matters more here than in a normal service. hermes-data/ holds the agent
# volume — .env with the Mistral key and the API server key, and after a first
# run the agent's own credential files — and .venv/ is tens of megabytes. Both
# would otherwise be uploaded to the Docker daemon (and to any remote builder)
# on every build, even though the Dockerfile never COPYs them.
*
!app/
!requirements.txt

# No compiled cruft from the allowed directories either.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
